Metric Types in Prometheus
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Understand the four core metric types in Prometheus: counter, gauge, histogram, and summary
Write effective Prometheus queries (PromQL) to demonstrate each metric type
Set up and configure a sample application that exposes different metric types
Collect and analyze metrics from a running application using Prometheus
Interpret the behavior and use cases for each metric type through hands-on practice
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with text editors (nano, vim, or similar)
Basic knowledge of HTTP concepts and web services
Understanding of monitoring concepts and time-series data
Completion of previous Prometheus labs or equivalent knowledge
